    "bounding box" : [ 28.6, 512.664, 204.687, 518.5 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(c) Mining. There is no doubt that, in proportion to its area,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.8, 506.766, 204.193, 512.408 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "the metalliferous wealth of the Isle of Man has been very consider-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 54,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 219.8, 502.417, 397.438, 508.642 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Law. The High Court of Justice, of which the licutenant-governor"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.8, 501.166, 205.348, 507.197 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "able. Two of its mines, Laxey and Foxdale, have stood for a long"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 55,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 213.4, 490.811, 397.953, 502.253 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "is president, contains three divisions: viz. the Chancery Division, in which the clerk of the rolls sits as judge, the Common Law Divi-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.6, 495.366, 204.096, 501.202 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "series of years in the first rank in the British Islands for productive-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.8, 489.566, 204.276, 495.013 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "ness of zinc and silver lead respectively. These metals have con-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 56,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.8, 444.41, 399.978, 490.754 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "sion, of which the deemsters are the judges, the Staff of Government Division, in which the governor and three judges sit together. The jurisdiction of the Chancery and Common Law Division is in the main similar to that of the corresponding divisions in the English Courts. The Staff of Government exercises appellate jurisdiction, similar to that of the Appeal Courts in England. The Common Law Courts for the southern division of the island are held at Douglas and Castletown alternately and those for the nor-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.4, 483.874, 204.38, 489.71 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "stituted its principal riches, but copper pyrites and hematite iron have"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 21.2, 478.078, 206.6, 483.72 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "also been raised in marketable quantities, while only very small:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.6, 454.89, 204.496, 478.126 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "amounts of the ores of nickel and antimony have been found.  The mines are rented from the Crown as lord of the manor. The value of the ore produced is about £40,000 annually. Other economic products are clay, granite, limestone, sandstone, slate (of an inferior"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.6, 449.182, 205.529, 454.824 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "quay) and salt, which has been discovered near the Point of"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 25.2, 443.397, 32.043, 449.428 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "yre"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 57,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 213.0, 438.61, 397.712, 444.057 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "thern division at Ramsey, once in three months. Actions in these"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 27.2, 437.597, 204.306, 443.044 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(d) Textiles, &c. Since labour: has become scarcer and dearer"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 58,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.8, 415.503, 398.335, 438.646 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "courts are heard by a deemster and a special or common jury. The Chancery Court sits once a fortnight at Douglas. The deemsters also have summary jurisdiction in matters of debt, actions for liquidated damages under £50, suits for possession of real or personal"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 420.197, 204.075, 437.439 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "textile industries have been declining, being unable to compete with larger and more completely organized manufactories elsewhere. The principal manufactured articles are woollen cloths and blankets,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 414.397, 204.014, 419.844 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "hemp ropes and cotton, and herring nets. A few fishing vessels"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 59,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 213.0, 409.703, 396.437, 415.345 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "property, petitions for probate, &c. These courts, called Deem-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 408.597, 203.931, 414.239 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "are built, and brewing is a prosperous industry. But, apart from"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 60,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.8, 403.796, 396.537, 409.632 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "sters  Courts, are held weekly, alternately at Douglas and Castletown,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 402.797, 203.741, 408.633 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "agriculture, the most important industry (for so it may be called)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 61,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.8, 397.996, 396.446, 403.443 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "by the deemster for the southern division of the island, and at Ram-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 396.904, 205.318, 402.546 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "is that of the provision for summer visitors, nearly half a million of"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 62,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.6, 374.796, 397.715, 398.032 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "sey and Peel by the deemster for the northern division. Criminal cases are heard by the magistrates or a high-bailiff and are (with the exception of minor cases which may be dealt with summarily) sent on by them for trial by a deemster and a jury of six; who hear the"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.4, 391.197, 150.683, 396.45 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.25,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "whom come to the island annually. :"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.0, 379.505, 204.07, 391.255 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Commerce- The chief exports are lead, zinc, turnips, ropes, cotton nets and salt. The imports consist chiefly of timber, pro-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.0, 373.813, 204.529, 379.455 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "visions, live-stock, poultry, flour, fruit, vegetables and eggs. In"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 63,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.6, 369.089, 397.079, 375.314 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "evidence and determine whether there is sufficient ground for sending"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.6, 368.106, 203.243, 373.942 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "1906 the tonnage of vessels (other than fishing or wind-bound vessels)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 64,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.6, 351.796, 398.876, 369.032 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "the case for trial before the Court of General Gaol Delivery, thus discharging the functions of the Grand Jury in England. The Court of General Gaol Delivery isthe Supreme Criminal Court and is"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
