    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.0, 362.305, 203.831, 367.752 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "cleared for traffic was 720,790. The number of vessels (other than"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 27,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 20.0, 356.398, 204.257, 362.234 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "fishing vessels) registered as belonging to the island in 1906 was 79."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 65,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.4, 340.103, 397.037, 351.545 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "presided over by the lieutenant-governor, who is assisted by the clerk of the rolls and the two deemsters. The high-bailiffs hold weekly"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 26.4, 344.997, 204.667, 351.222 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Government. The government of the island is vested in a"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 29,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.8, 330.597, 204.717, 343.828 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "lieutenant-governor, appointed by the Crown; in a Council, which is the upper branch of the legislature; in the House of"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 66,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.4, 334.303, 397.077, 340.334 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "courts in the four towns for the recovery of debts under forty shillings"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 67,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.4, 322.81, 396.704, 334.145 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "and for the trial of cases usually brought before a stipendiary magistrate in England. The magistrates (J.P. s) also hold regular courts"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 30,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.6, 316.104, 203.441, 329.529 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Keys, which is the lower branch; and in the Tynwald Court. The Council and Keys sit separately as legislative bodies,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 68,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.2, 288.01, 397.245, 322.939 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "in the towns for the trial of breaches of the peace and minor offences. There is a coroner in each of the six sheadings.. These officers are appointed annually by the lieutenant-governor and perform duties similar to those of a sheriff's officer in England. Inquests of death are held by a high-bailiff and jury. The Manx Bar is distinct from that of England. Its»members, called Advocates,   combine the"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 31,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.6, 308.889, 203.296, 315.309 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "but they sit in the Tynwald Court as distinct bodies with"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 32,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.0, 279.996, 204.165, 307.914 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "co-ordinate powers to transact executive business and to sign Bills. The Tynwald Court controls the surplus revenue, after the payment of the cost of government and of a fixed contribution of £10,000 to the imperial exchequer, subject to the super-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 69,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.2, 282.103, 396.67, 288.134 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "functions of barrister and solicitor. The laws relating to real pro-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 70,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 264.796, 396.147, 282.139 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "perty still retain much of their ancient peculiarity, but other branches of law have of late years by various acts of Tynwald been made practically identical with English law."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 33,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.4, 272.796, 202.51, 278.827 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "vision of the Treasury and the veto of the lieutenant-governor,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 34,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.4, 265.489, 203.075, 271.714 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
